2026-04-19 10:40:11,961 [nexau.archs.main_sub.execution.tool_executor] INFO: 🔧 Executing tool 'write_file' for agent 'agent_f0b7dec0' with parameters: {'content': '# Proposer Reasoning — Candidate 1\n\n## What Changed\nReplaced the dummy baseline model (returns zeros) with an ensemble of MLP + GradientBoosting, incorporating:\n\n1. **MLP with BatchNorm + SmoothL1Loss + OneCycleLR** — the architecture that achieved the highest score (37.4) across all prior evolution runs (hoss-evolution-2).\n2. **GradientBoostingRegressor** — a complementary tree-based model that captures non-linear feature interactions differently from the MLP, improving ensemble diversity.\n3. **StandardScaler normalization** — normalizes all features before feeding to both models.\n4. **Sequence-structure interaction features** — 11 additional engineered features:\n   - seq_norm, seq_mean, seq_std (summary statistics of the 320-dim ESM embedding)\n   - struct_product, struct_ratio (interactions between atom_count and residue_count)\n   - 6 cross-modal interactions (each struct feature × each seq summary stat)\n5. **Adaptive ensemble weight calibration** — grid search over MLP/GBR blending weight using Pearson correlation on training data.\n\n## Why This Should Improve Score\n- The baseline returns zeros → any trained model is a massive improvement.\n- The MLP architecture (BatchNorm + SmoothL1Loss + OneCycleLR) was the single best-performing approach across 3 evolution runs, peaking at F1=0.374 (score 37.4).\n- Adding GBR as an ensemble partner provides complementary predictions — tree models and neural nets have different inductive biases, so their errors are partially uncorrelated.\n- Feature engineering creates explicit cross-modal interactions that help both models leverage the relationship between sequence embeddings and structure features.\n- StandardScaler helps the MLP converge better and the GBR handle features at different scales.\n\n## Expected Impact\n- Baseline score: 0 (dummy model)\n- Expected score: 37+ (based on evolution-2 MLP achieving 37.4, plus ensemble and feature engineering improvements)\n- Target: >38 final_score\n', 'file_path': '/inspire/qb-ilm/project/cq-scientific-cooperation-zone/public/ywang/meta-harness-evolver/project/project-2-simple-split-model/hoss-evolution-claude/candidates/candidate_1/proposer_reasoning.md'}
