out the sequence-structure relationship.\\n\\n## Expected Impact\\n- Should significantly exceed the dummy baseline (score 0).\\n- Target: match or exceed the best prior score of 37.4, potentially reaching 38-40+ through the ensemble and feature engineering improvements.\\n", "file_path": "/inspire/qb-ilm/project/cq-scientific-cooperation-zone/public/ywang/meta-harness-evolver/project/project-2-simple-split-model/hoss-evolution-claude/candidates/candidate_1/proposer_reasoning.md"}'}}]}, {'role': 'tool', 'tool_call_id': 'tooluse_tWB4xHNyouzdmOK7L9PVqU', 'content': '{\n  "content": "Successfully created and wrote to new file: /inspire/qb-ilm/project/cq-scientific-cooperation-zone/public/ywang/meta-harness-evolver/project/project-2-simple-split-model/hoss-evolution-claude/candidates/candidate_1/proposer_reasoning.md."\n}'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'tool_calls': [{'id': 'tooluse_ZU6MBgHejbm4PsEJStMKoV', 'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'write_file', 'arguments': '{"content": "# Proposer Reasoning — Candidate 1\\n\\n## What Changed\\nReplaced the dummy baseline model (returns zeros) with an ensemble of MLP + GradientBoosting, incorporating:\\n\\n1. **MLP with BatchNorm + SmoothL1Loss + OneCycleLR** — the architecture that achieved the highest score (37.4) across all prior evolution runs (hoss-evolution-2).\\n2. **GradientBoostingRegressor** — a complementary tree-based model that captures non-linear feature interactions differently from the MLP, improving ensemble diversity.\\n3. **StandardScaler normalization** — normalizes all features before feeding to both models.\\n4. **Sequence-structure interaction features** — 11 additional engineered features:\\n   - seq_norm, seq_mean, seq_std (summary statistics of the 320-dim ESM embedding)\\n   - struct_product, struct_ratio (interactions between atom_count and residue_count)\\n   - 6 cross-modal interactions (each struct feature × each seq summary stat)\\n5. **Adaptive ensemble weight calibration** — grid search over MLP/GBR blending weight using Pearson correlation on training data.\\n\\n## Why This Should Improve Score\\n- The baseline returns zeros → any trained model is a massive improvement.\\n- The MLP architecture (BatchNorm + SmoothL1Loss + OneCycleLR) was the single best-performing approach across 3 evolution runs, peaking at F1=0.374 (score 37.4).\\n- Adding GBR as an ensemble partner provides complementary predictions — tree models and neural nets have different inductive biases, so their errors are partially uncorrelated.\\n- Feature engineering creates explicit cross-modal interactions that help both models leverage the relationship between sequence embeddings and structure features.\\n- StandardScaler helps the MLP converge better and the GBR handle features at different scales.\\n\\n## Expected Impact\\n- Baseline score: 0 (dummy model)\\n- Expected score: 37+ (based on evolution-2 MLP achieving 37.4, plus ensemble and feature engineering improvements)\\n- Target: >38 final_score\\n", "file_path": "/inspire/qb-ilm/project/cq-scientific-cooperation-zone/public/ywang/meta-harness-evolver/project/project-2-simple-split-model/hoss-evolution-claude/candidates/candidate_1/proposer_reasoning.md"}'}}]}, {'role': 'tool', 'tool_call_id': 'tooluse_ZU6MBgHejbm4PsEJStMKoV', 'content': '{\n  "content": "Successfully overwrote file: /inspire/qb-ilm/project/cq-scientific-cooperation-zone/public/ywang/meta-harness-evolver/project/project-2-simple-split-model/hoss-evolution-claude/candidates/candidate_1/proposer_reasoning.md."\n}'}], 'model': 'claude-opus-4-6', 'max_tokens': 2048, 'temperature': 0.2, 'tool_choice': 'auto', 'tools': [{'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'WebSearch', 'description': '- Allows Claude to search the web and use the results to inform responses - Provides up-to-date information for current events and recent data - Returns search result information formatted as search result blocks - Use this tool for accessing information beyond Claude\'s knowledge cu